<title>BELGIUM: Italian economy going in right direction - de Silguy.</title>
<headline>Italian economy going in right direction - de Silguy.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Monetary Affairs Commissioner Yves Thibault de Silguy said on Wednesday that Italy's economy was moving in the right direction ahead of economic and monetary union.</p>
<p>&quot;The situation in Italy seems to be moving in the right direction and I think that is encouraging,&quot; de Silguy told the European Parliament.</p>
<p>He reiterated that the &quot;moment of truth&quot; for the Italian government's hopes of qualifying for the single curreency would come in the autumn with its 1998 budget. -- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
